<section class="disclaimer-box" aria-labelledby="fresno-jurisdiction-heading" id="city-or-county">
	<h2 id="fresno-jurisdiction-heading">City of Fresno or Fresno County?</h2>
	<p>They have separate permit offices and application portals. Confirm which office handles your property before applying.</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>City of Fresno:</strong> the <a href={citySolar}>City's SolarAPP+ instructions</a> direct registered, licensed contractors to upload their approval confirmation to City Accela. The <a href={cityBuilding}>City Building and Safety page</a> links to application search, status and inspections.</li>
		<li><strong>Fresno County:</strong> use the <a href={countySolar}>County's official solar permit instructions</a> and <a href={countyPortal}>County permit portal</a>. The County issues the building permit; SolarAPP+ confirmation alone is not a building permit.</li>
	</ul>
	<p><small>Links and pathway summary checked October 28, 2026. GridPermit is an independent guide, not either permit office.</small></p>
</section>
